                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Operator directive (2026-06-30): replace HFST_THROW/HFST_THROW_MESSAGE + panic_any/catch_unwind + the ~30 Hfst*Exception structs with a proper Result<T, HfstError>, and DROP the \"Exception\" nomenclature entirely. Surface: 154 HFST_THROW + 106 HFST_THROW_MESSAGE + 107 direct panic_any (~382 throw sites) + 24 catch_unwind across ~24 files; 443 Exception identifier refs. Design (hand-rolled, no thiserror — avoids a network dep, matches house minimal-dep style; mirrors divvunspell's TransducerError intent): pub struct HfstError { kind: HfstErrorKind, message: Option<String> } + enum HfstErrorKind with one variant per former exception (suffix dropped: FunctionNotImplemented, TransducerTypeMismatch, ImplementationTypeNotAvailable(ImplementationType), NotValidAttFormat, Fatal [was HfstFatal], ...), impl Display/Error, pub type HfstResult<T>; ergonomic hfst_bail!(Kind) / hfst_bail!(Kind, msg) macros that `return Err(...)`. Migration = leaf-up, staged by subsystem with the 151 tests as oracle: convert deepest throwing fns to return HfstResult, ripple `?` to callers; a bridge (panic_to_result at catch boundaries, or .expect() at not-yet-converted callers) keeps each stage green. Sequenced as foundational for the idiom5 symbol-coding keystone (its get_symbol throws today): do the error model, then K2/K3 uses Result. K1 of the keystone (SymbolCoder/FormatCoder encapsulation) is banked."
            }
        )
    }

    {
        id idiom7
        title "Stage 7 — adopt `tracing` for all diagnostic logging in the hfst lib. The library must not write diagnostics to stderr directly; it emits `tracing` events (warn!/error!/info!/debug!/trace!) and the application owns the subscriber. DATA output (att/dot writers, lookup results, xfst REPL result text to stdout) and interactive prompts are NOT logging and stay as direct I/O. Oracle: 152 hfst tests."
        children (
            {
                id idiom7.warning-stream-tracing
                title "Replace the WARNING_STREAM global sink with `tracing`. The per-backend thread_local Option&lt;Box&lt;dyn Write&gt;&gt; (tropical + log) is written at exactly one site — check_epsilon_cycles' \"transducer has epsilon cycles with a negative weight\" warning. Emit `tracing::warn!` there instead; delete the WARNING_STREAM thread_local, set_warning_stream + with_warning_stream (both backends) and the facade set_warning_stream. The 2 CLI callers (hfst-eliminate-flags, hfst-remove-epsilons) drop set_warning_stream and install a tracing-subscriber fmt-to-stderr so the warning still renders. Removes the last per-thread mutable sink; establishes the tracing pattern. Oracle: 152 hfst tests."
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-06-30T16:16:53.929703Z
