                        id upstream-bugs.t1.i571
                        title "hfst#571: 'regexp2fst [] -> a || _' mis-compiles (empty-language LHS in replace rule inserts wrongly) — xerox-rules replace compilation (hfst_xerox_rules.rs); compare against Xerox insertion semantics"
                        priority 1
                        log (
                            {
                                at 2026-07-10T23:03:08.358027Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "INVESTIGATED (opus, 2026-07-11): REPRODUCES — byte-identical to upstream's buggy output; genuine still-open upstream defect faithfully ported. '[] -> a || _' builds a 2-state machine forcing exactly one 'a' insertion at EVERY position mandatorily and DROPS identity (xy -> axaya only; '' -> a). '[]', '0', '[..]', '[. .]' all parse to XreExpr::Epsilon (xre.rs:2252-2260, :329/:757) so the center is @0@:a; then replace_rule (hfst_xerox_rules.rs:2305-2340) applies most_brackets_star_constraint (:2331, only when !optional) making insertion obligatory everywhere — 1:1 mirror of HfstXeroxRules.cc:706-717/:2402-2437. CORRECT semantics (established via the optional arrow, which WORKS): '[] (->) a || _' gives free insertion at all positions WITH identity preserved (xy -> {xy, axy, xay, xya, axay, axya, xaya, axaya}) per Beesley-Karttunen p.175-176; context-full '[] -> a || b _ c' also already correct. FIX (M): epsilon-LHS + empty/universal-context detection in replace_rule (+siblings :2345/:2398/:2465) forcing the optional path (skip most_brackets_star_constraint); guard must evaluate AFTER Rule::encode_flags() so encoded flags in a context aren't misread as empty (flag-complement audit deferral interaction). CAUTION: test7h (test_xerox_rules.rs:2371, '[..] @-> a') asserts the BUGGY golden FST and must be migrated; test6a (:1830, '0 -> p || m _ k') is the boundary guardrail that must NOT change. Deliberate divergence -> spec bump in the xerox-rules doc. DEFER: distinguishing Xerox [..] single-insertion semantics from []/0 (parser-side, wider blast radius) — scope to obligatory-vs-optional only."
                            }

