            {
                id rustfst-determinize-table
                title "Compact rustfst determinize subset table (arena-flattened tuples, raw-entry hash); attacks lexc 750 MiB floor + pmatch compile plateau; instrument first"
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-18T01:34:56.162694Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "DESIGN (2026-07-18, from reading the fork at ~/git/necessary/rustfst, branch fix/determinize-subset-canonicalization): determinize's live memory = (a) the state table (state_table.rs): id_to_tuple: Vec<Arc<DeterminizeStateTuple>> + tuple_to_id: HashMap<Arc<DeterminizeStateTuple>, StateId, FxHash> — one Arc'd tuple per OUTPUT state, alive for the whole run (a re-reached subset must map to the same id, so nothing is droppable); (b) the growing output VectorFst (per-state Arc<Vec<Tr>> COW — load-bearing, CSR retired in a0bda95); (c) the input FST. Per-tuple cost: Arc header 16 B + WeightedSubset Vec header 24 B + 8 B per element (StateId u32 + TropicalWeight f32) + hash-map entry ~24-32 B + id_to_tuple slot 8 B ≈ 72 B + 8·|subset| per output state. COMPACTION: flatten all subset elements into one arena Vec<(StateId, W)>; a tuple becomes (offset u32, len u32, filter_state) in id_to_tuple (16 B, no Arc, no per-tuple allocation); dedup via hashbrown raw-entry keyed by hashing the arena slice (fxhash already in-tree). Kills ~40-56 B/tuple fixed overhead + allocator churn, improves probe locality. Transient DeterminizeTr dest_tuples (owned subsets during expansion, determinize_fsa_op.rs) stay as-is or borrow from a scratch arena. NO unsafe needed (raw_entry is safe API). STEP 1 — INSTRUMENT BEFORE DESIGN-FREEZE: add counters (peak tuple count, total elements, avg/max |subset|) behind a feature or tracing to the fork and run the lexc oracle compile (750 MiB peak, ~1M-state encoded machines) + a pmatch morphoword compile; if the table is <20% of peak the lever is dead and the floor is the output-FST + input residency (then close honestly like rustfst-trsvec-csr / pmatch-encode-weights). Validation: lexc sha256 34f2debe... byte-oracle + hfst 291 tests + rustfst's own suite; land via the fork (see [[rustfst-now-editable]]). Affects every determinize/minimize user: lexc floor (750 MiB), pmatch compile plateau (~3.5 GiB), compose-intersect's piped minimize."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-18T01:44:22.886671Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan_start)"
                    }

