                        text "DESIGN (from 2026-07-18 CPU-true profiling; full data in agent memory lang-sma-memory-profile): a representative src/fst xfst derivation script spends ~15% of main-thread samples in dfs_visit/connect driven by property RECOMPUTATION — rustfst acceptor_minimize opens with compute_and_update_properties(ACCEPTOR|UNWEIGHTED|ACYCLIC), and those bits arrive unknown every time because (1) the encode mapper (encode_static.rs properties()) provably makes the machine an ACCEPTOR when encode_labels (ilabel/olabel fused into one label) and UNWEIGHTED when encode_weights (weights folded into labels, all outputs One) but never SETS either bit — it only masks; (2) determinize_properties (faithful to OpenFST) propagates ACYCLIC/ACCEPTOR from input but not weightedness. Setting bits that are true by construction is sound and cannot change output bytes (same argument as the landed trim-gated connect, fork 4757976e). Sequence per TWT::minimize today: RmEpsilon -> Encode(labels) -> Determinize -> rustfst minimize [compute_and_update FULL SCC DFS -> push/shortest_distance -> Encode(weights+labels) -> acceptor_minimize -> decode] -> Decode. The compute_and_update DFS is the killable part. Validate: lexc sha ea98a54c + tokeniser cmp 541,169,926 + speller xfst artifact cmp + 291 tests. Est ~10-15s off the 200s build."
                    }

