                        kind @note
                        text "PHASE-1 GATE FAILED — NEGATIVE VERDICT, do not wire foma into pmatch2fst. Probe: crates/hfst/examples/pmatch_backend_probe.rs (kept as regression probe). FEASIBILITY (all confirmed): PmatchCompiler::<FomaTransducer> IS instantiable (FomaTransducer: AlgebraBackend+FromAnyTransducer+'static, hfst_transducer.rs:4307); @bin tropical inputs convert via into_typed→any_into_backend_via_basic; write_archive<B> is generic. BUT the hypothesis is false on two independent axes:\n\n(1) DIRECT MEASUREMENT (weighttest mode on the real tokeniser-disamb-gt-desc.pmscript): tropical TOP = 561,370 states / 22,855,366 arcs. Zero ALL weights (transform_weights(|_|0.0)+set_final_weights(0.0)) then minimize → 561,309 states / 22,846,860 arcs. That is a 0.011% state / 0.037% arc reduction — the \"weight-diversity inflation\" premise is FALSE. Arc count is inherent to the composed analyser-over-sigma machine, NOT weights. Independently corroborates the retired encode_weights lever (lang-sma-memory-profile: hfst-minimize -E merges nothing).\n\n(2) write_archive HARDCODES weighted=true (pmatch_compiler.rs:6787-6825), so even a foma-compiled TOP writes 12-byte-transition weighted OLW. On-disk transition widths: TransitionW=12B, Transition(unweighted)=8B, index entries 6B in both. Max possible de-weighting win = 22.85M×4B ≈ 87 MB = 16% of the 541 MB archive, and ONLY achievable via a SEPARATE write_archive(weighted=false) change (which changes the runtime OLW format hfst-tokenise expects). Structural floor stays ~429 MB.\n\n(3) BLOCKER even to measure foma directly: PmatchCompiler::<FomaTransducer>.compile PANICS on this pmscript — foma-0.4.0/src/constructions/merge_sigma.rs expand_unknowns undersizes the arc buffer (add_fsm_arc index 728 == len 728), reached via UpCase(lexmorph,U)→toupper→FomaTransducer::compose. Diagnosed: the count loop counts net_lines via find_arccount (arcs only) but the write loop RE-EMITS arc-less state-marker rows (line_in==-1, merge_sigma.rs:259-271) that aren't counted → overshoot by #arc-less-states. Real off-by-N bug in the foma crate (registry v0.4.0 == local ~/git/necessary/foma HEAD). NB the memory's \"foma is a path-dep\" is stale — hfst now uses the published crate foma=\"0.4\".\n\nMEASUREMENTS: tropical compile-only 561,370/22,855,366 (matches historical 561,562/22,852,267 within input-regen noise), 57s, 4.37 GB RSS. weighttest 37s, 4.73 GB RSS. foma compile panics at 1.97s/207 MB. Existing tropical .pmhfst = 541,471,216 B. Recommendation: retire this node OR redefine it as an explicit SUCCESSOR-divergence to emit UNWEIGHTED OL archives (needs write_archive(weighted=false) + hfst-tokenise read-compat) for a ~16% ceiling — a much smaller, riskier prize than the 541→~small the node assumed. Left UNCOMMITTED for the main session."
