                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Fixed on nplan/panic-on-malformed-input (2fe3c92), merged as 8f49b7a. Verified here: `hfst tokenize <plain .hfstol>` now emits \"ab\" and exits 0 where it panicked at pmatch.rs:2724; `hfst pmatch <plain .hfstol>` exits 1 with \"not a pmatch archive: the transducer's alphabet carries no @PMATCH_ENTRY@/@PMATCH_EXIT@ markers\"; 334/334 workspace and 247/247 --features foma.\n\nROOT CAUSE, deeper than the two sites I filed and worth remembering: both panics are ONE bug. A state's index-table probe is `state + input_symbol`, and the OL writer pads the index table with one blank entry per INPUT symbol — but identity, unknown and output-only symbols are numbered ABOVE input_symbol_count, so a probe can legitimately exceed the padding. An empty transducer has seen_input_symbols == 1 (epsilon only) and a 2-entry index table, yet its alphabet still holds @_IDENTITY_SYMBOL_@/@_UNKNOWN_SYMBOL_@, so get_analyses routes unmatched input to find_index(identity_symbol) -> index_table[2]. pmatch probes further still because PmatchContainer builds its encoder over orig_symbol_count rather than input_symbol_count. C++ read past the vector and got a non-matching entry; get_transitions_from_state (transducer.rs:2669) already guarded its probe with exactly this reasoning, so the fix follows in-tree precedent.\n\nDESIGN ANSWER to the question I posed: empty RESULT, not Err. An empty transducer is a value and the empty language accepts nothing, so Err would be wrong for compose_intersect's callers. Returning the blank padding entry is what a correctly-padded table would have given, so nothing is lost — the out-of-range probes are only ever for symbols with no arcs. Err is reserved for input that cannot hold together: bad targets/symbols, impossible header (input_symbol_count > symbol_count), wrong file type.\n\nAlso hardened at the read boundary: tables cross-validated against each other and the alphabet in load_tables / PmatchTransducer::new_from_stream (this is what catches the original \"len is 2 but the index is 897\" .hfstol), table reads batched at 64Ki entries so a corrupt size field stops at a short read rather than a 48 GB allocation, and an empty-string alphabet symbol no longer walks the encoder trie off a one-byte buffer.\n\nFOLLOW-THROUGH: the agent un-deferred the assertion in compose_intersect_with_no_rules_is_empty, which I had written structurally (number_of_arcs) precisely because this defect made accepts() unusable. It now asserts non-acceptance directly, as that node's log said it should once this was fixed."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-12T09:14:32.188148Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
